                "Five things protect profits in this group, and the grid grades each company on each one; what each business does is explained in Tab 2. The short version: switching costs are high almost everywhere, because this software sits inside banks' lending desks, loyalty ledgers, warehouses and government registers. What separates the companies is whether that stickiness turns into pricing power and cash, and whether the company is run and reported cleanly. On that basis the strongest moats are Newgen, Capillary, Unicommerce's core and Protean; the weakest are TAC, NPST and IZMO.",
