                    text: "Lending, document and transaction-banking software is rarely replaced. **Nucleus** says FinnOne installations two decades old are still running, and HDFC Bank has used its software for about 30 years. **Intellect** earns ₹585cr a year of maintenance and ₹595cr of platform fees from 500+ institutions, and about 80–85% of its business comes from existing clients. **Newgen**'s annuity revenue rose from 56% to 62% of revenue in FY26 even as Indian licence sales fell 20–30%, which shows the installed base paying through a bad year. The moat is not absolute: **Nucleus** lost Bajaj Finance to a rival that Bajaj had invested in, and admitted in Q1 that ‘some of the logos have left’. My view: this is the most durable moat in the group, but it protects revenue more than price, because banks negotiate hard at renewal.",
